    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks. the issue is that i'm seeing some really sharp, almost erratic spikes in the salinity readings at certain depths that don't seem to correlate with the temperature drop. it almost looks like the sensor is glitching or we've got some localized anomalies. how should i differentiate between actual physical saline plumes and just sensor noise or data errors?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
