      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "To differentiate between real plumes and noise, first, examine the temporal consistency of the spikes; true plumes will be sustained or show a pattern, unlike random noise. Compare the anomalous salinity readings against nearby, stable temperature measurements to see if the density change is proportional to what the temperature suggests. Finally, review the raw sensor diagnostics and check calibration logs to rule out instrument malfunction before concluding a physical anomaly.",
